      }
    ],
    "status": "present",
    "value": "Sort intervals by end ascending and, for equal ends, by start descending. Process them in that order and remember the two largest chosen points, first < second. If an interval starts after second, it contains none of the chosen points, so add its two rightmost integers end-1 and end. If it starts after first but not after second, it contains only second, so add end. Otherwise it already has two. Choosing points as far right as possible maximises their chance of lying in later intervals, which all end at or after the current one."
  },
